## Error handling
- If test_event_changelist_defaults_to_draft_filter fails (both events visible): verify the
  changelist_view method uses request.GET.copy() (mutable QueryDict) before setting
  status__exact. Django's GET is immutable -- direct assignment without .copy() silently
  fails in some Django versions.
- If test_consent_captured_on_first_publish fails (consent_recorded_at is None): verify the
  save_model method calls super().save_model() before checking status transition, and that
  the event's organizer FK in the POST data is the same organizer being checked.
- If the change_form.html template is not found (falls back to default): verify the file is
  at /workspace/templates/admin/events/event/change_form.html (not inside any app's templates
  dir) and that TEMPLATES[0]['DIRS'] includes /workspace/templates (confirmed line 82).
- If /admin/events/event/ returns 302 to login page: ensure test uses force_login(superuser)
  and the user has is_superuser=True (create_superuser guarantees this).

